<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!-- Configuration file. All simulation parameters values must be put here. -->
<!-- Scaled-up scenario (20 RRHs / 10 Edge nodes / 1 Cloud, 2 RRHs/Edge),
     grounded in the parameters the group's own prior Cloud-Fog work used as its state of the
     art (old/graph.py, old/simulator.py - Tinini et al. 2019, cited in README.md):
       - CPRI line rate 614 Mbps per RRH (old/graph.py: cpri_line) - the per-RRH reference load unit.
       - fogs=10 (old/graph.py) - reused here as the Edge node count.
       - fog:cloud capacity ratio 1:10 (old/graph.py) - reused directionally (Edge << Cloud).
       - fog/cloud activation cost 300/600 and fog/cloud access delay (old/graph.py: costs,
         fog_delay, cloud_delay) - unchanged from the Test Sample scenario.
     Edge capacity=2, RRHs/Edge=2: each RRH's placement candidates are
     restricted by simulation.py (MAX_CANDIDATE_HOPS) to its local Edge/ring-neighbors + Cloud,
     not every Edge network-wide - found while validating this scale-up to be necessary for
     stability (a globally-competing heuristic flooded ring transit traffic well before any
     Edge's own capacity was the bottleneck). See scripts/run_load_sweep.py for how far this
     RRHs/Edge ratio can grow before the system stops keeping up in real time. -->

